    "claimsDirectlyCompared": [
      "Scores are one motivation alongside progress, items and ranking.",
      "A metric name and scale can frame what a player thinks the number means.",
      "Brain Age/Wii Fit examples use age as a presentation frame, not proof of real cognitive or health change.",
      "Opaque game-deviation formulas show why an appealing metric also needs interpretable criteria.",
      "Burnout uses fictional damage-money units; these are not real losses.",
      "Smash Global Smash Power is a comparative performance frame.",
      "The final discussion returns to how a score is displayed and counted up."
